# Force LF line endings on checkout for all text files in the
# FlatBuffers family, regardless of the contributor's OS / git
# autocrlf setting. The published .fbs files always end in LF (the
# formatter enforces it), and the tests compare corpus content
# byte-for-byte through template literals — CRLF checkout on Windows
# would silently fail those tests.
#
# Scoped here (git applies .gitattributes per directory tree) so the
# rule doesn't impose LF on unrelated sibling projects.
* text=auto eol=lf
